(Results) Tj T*
(A chromosome segment substitution line, SL14, showed higher survival than the recurrent parent) Tj T*
(WY after 12 h of heat treatment \(fig. S1\). We backcrossed SL14 to WY to construct a mapping) Tj T*
(population. Using 1,614 BC4F3 plants from this population, qHT3 was narrowed to a 36.6 kb) Tj T*
(interval on chromosome 3 \(Table 1\). Only recombinant plants that survived the heat treatment) Tj T*
(were advanced to the next generation.) Tj T*
(Table 1 Fine mapping of qHT3) Tj T*
(Interval Markers Size) Tj T*
(qHT3 M11-M19 36.6 kb) Tj T*
(To test whether HTR1 underlies qHT3, we generated knockout lines of HTR1 in WY by CRISPR/Cas9.) Tj T*
(The knockout lines of HTR1 showed lower survival than WY after heat treatment \(fig. S2\). We) Tj T*
(hypothesized that HTR1 might recruit HTR2 precursors to endosomes for degradation. HTR1) Tj T*
(interacted with HTR2 in a split-luciferase assay \(fig. S3\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Discussion) Tj T*
(These results indicate that HTR1 acts upstream of HTR2 to protect chloroplasts under heat) Tj T*
(stress. How HTR2 accumulation damages chloroplasts remains to be determined. Materials and) Tj T*
(methods are available as supplementary materials.) Tj T*
ET
